"""Items part 3: the weapons, the mission items file, the module lifecycle, props, frame trees

Sources: M items_module.cpp, D item_defs.cpp, I item_instances.cpp, C item_containers.cpp (labels: letter + line).
Run: set MUT_HARNESS=items, MUT_EXTRA_SRCS=ls3df/src/math/math.cpp, MUT_EXTRA_INC=ls3df/src, then
python _re/harness/mutrun.py _re/harness/items/mutations/mutate_items3.py WORK [JOBS]. Needs ITEMS_SAV and
EQUIPMENT_SAVE (see build.bat).
Generated by _re/harness/shots/gen_mutations.py per source (lines unique in their file), merged.

Result (2026-11-10): 454 mutants; 398 killed, 33 not building, 23 survived:
- equivalent at the boundary (the same result either way): I 348 cmp (rounds at exactly 0), I 447 cmp (exactly full:
  no rest), I 474 / 476 cmp (the same ready time);
- data the table never has (no weapon uses ammunition type 1, no sound number 0): I 423 num, I 768 cmp, I 774 num / cmp;
- set again before it shows: I 580 del (the projectile, null already), I 732 num / del (the shot sound's position,
  replaced when it plays), M 1649 num (the version: a failed read returns first), M 1715 num / bool (the source
  container of a new item; notify while the mission is switched off);
- leaks with nothing to see: M 226 del (a definition not deleted), M 1638 del (the placements' old block), M 1720 del
  (an item without an actor);
- unreachable: M 1726 num / del (a new item never displaces one, so the "displaced" message never shows);
- out of range in the fakes only: M 1598 cmp (the actors' list read one past its end), M 1602 num / 1608 num (a
  vehicle's container 1, an item slot's slots: the fakes answer null);
- M 1662 arith: a 128-character name read into the 128-byte buffer (undefined behaviour; the test sees no difference).
First run: 324 killed, 97 survived; added since: Init on a used weapon, the reload boundaries (container 6, space 0.5,
equal magazines, the launcher's contents), the sounds' details, the clock wrapping for StopReloadSound, the frame
trees released for real, the module's uids and Done, the mission file's failures and boundaries.
Checked against the original's asm: Reload's magazine selection and the rest (0x007d4ee3..0x007d5030), the mission
file's name read (nameLength + 1 bytes, 0x007d87ae).
"""
